                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "39189723",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198005172375",
                            "num_reviews": 9,
                            "playtime_forever": 7,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 7,
                            "last_played": 1515439343
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I personally thought this games difficulty is more due to bad design, there is a reason why all achievements have only been accessed by such a small amount of owners of this game. The poor controls are also a major factor in this. Controls are also not even key bindable (to my knowledge). Double jump should never be holding space, I am amazed I have to say that.\n\nI would also like to criticise the fact that the settings are not made available via the main menu and only via pausing the game, this was not known to me at first, and this was not helped by the fact that the music after only a few minutes was beginning to grate in my skull and that the graphics settings (also only accessible via main menu) decided to go on the highest possible setting by default, despite that causing a notable frame rate issue.\n\nI only paid 20p for this game due to a coupon per badge crafting, and after maybe 10 minutes at most am personally in the mood to refund.\n\nMaybe this game isn't meant for me, but I have a nagging feeling this game has flaws that need addressing.",
